{"format":"rerail.policy/v1","id":"eslint-no-sequences","revision":2,"mode":"steer","description":"Port of ESLint's `no-sequences` rule (https://eslint.org/docs/latest/rules/no-sequences). Default options (allowInParentheses: true): flags the comma operator except in for-loop init/update and when the sequence is wrapped in parentheses (doubled where the grammar already requires them). Options are declared in the `options` define (the rule's defaults); a variant is a config patch.","scope":{"include":["**/*"],"exclude":[]},"clauses":[{"id":"options","define":{"options":{"allowInParentheses":{"type":"boolean","nullable":true,"default":null}}}},{"id":"comma-operator","forbid":{"ast":{"language":"typescript","rule":{"regex":"^,$","not":{"follows":{"regex":"^,$","stopBy":"end"}},"inside":{"kind":"sequence_expression","stopBy":"neighbor","not":{"any":[{"matches":"for-init-or-update"},{"$option":"allowInParentheses","cases":{"false":[]},"default":[{"matches":"intent-parens"}],"spread":true}]}}},"utils":{"for-init-or-update":{"any":[{"inside":{"kind":"for_statement","stopBy":"neighbor"},"any":[{"follows":{"regex":"^\\($","stopBy":"neighbor"}},{"precedes":{"regex":"^\\)$","stopBy":"neighbor"}}]},{"inside":{"kind":"parenthesized_expression","stopBy":"neighbor","matches":"for-init-or-update"}}]},"intent-parens":{"inside":{"kind":"parenthesized_expression","stopBy":"neighbor","any":[{"not":{"inside":{"stopBy":"neighbor","any":[{"kind":"if_statement"},{"kind":"while_statement"},{"kind":"do_statement"},{"kind":"switch_statement"},{"kind":"with_statement"},{"kind":"arrow_function"}]}}},{"inside":{"kind":"parenthesized_expression","stopBy":"neighbor"}}]}}}}},"violation":{"anchor":"witness.span","code":"no-sequences","message":"Unexpected use of comma operator.","suppress":{"eslint":{"rules":["no-sequences"]},"oxlint":{"rules":["no-sequences"]}}}}]}
